<title>PARAGUAY: Rains endanger Paraguayan early wheat.</title>
<headline>Rains endanger Paraguayan early wheat.</headline>
<dateline>ASUNCION 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Heavy rains are putting 40 percent of Paraguay's early-variety wheat crop at risk, the Paraguayan Cereals Exporters Chamber said Thursday.</p>
<p>Some 20,000 hectares, or about 40 percent of the total early wheat crop area, have suffered after about 120 millimeters of rain over the last week.</p>
<p>Exporters hope to harvest about 400,000 tonnes of wheat in 1996, and expect to export about 100,000 tonnes to Brazil. But exports could suffer if rains continue, the chamber said.</p>
<p>Paraguayan farmers sowed a total 208,000 hectares with all wheat varieties this season, up from 172,000 hectares in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Jose Maria Amarilla, Asuncion Newsroom +595 44-4527</p>
